I didn't make this change. The requested simplification is the same one commit e92f1b2 reverted, and the reason for that revert still applies.

That commit's message says that with `chunked=` passed to `conn.urlopen`, uploads through an HTTP proxy hang forever (issue #42). The pool's chunked mode skips `proxy_pool` and never sends the terminating 0-length chunk. The manual framing in `send()` avoids this by switching to `conn.proxy_pool` and writing the `0\r\n\r\n` terminator itself. The revert says to keep it until the pool handles proxies, and `pool.py` here is only a stub, so I can't show that has changed.

If you know the pool now handles proxies, tell me and I'll make the change. I'd also add a proxy upload test to cover #42. Alternatively, I could leave the chunked path as it is and tidy it up without changing behavior, for example by extracting it into a `_send_chunked` helper.[INFO] [KRS] <-- GenerateAssistantResponseCommand done totalEvents=76

